; The record types Flow's Memory keeps that Operation names: how a launch
; request settled, kept beside its attempt so LaunchStatus and
; Observe.Launch answer it without running the launch again, and a
; replacement under way, the successor's launch request and the predecessor
; it reaps. SeatBirth is the seat a restart bound: the route it runs in and
; the birth of its harness process, kept after the restart's record goes, so
; an event of the seat it replaced is told from the seat's own.
;
; What a launch still owes once its flow is confirmed and receiving is
; kept as an obligation beside its outcome, each fact once. A PendingReap
; is the reap a replacement owes its predecessor, keyed by the predecessor:
; its pane closed and the Address's handover handed on; its successor is
; read through its launch's outcome, never copied here, and who owes it is
; recorded with it: the successor, a later flow that took it over, or the
; Address when nothing receives there. A PendingHandover
; is the handover a fresh launch owes at its Address, one at most per
; Address. Which flow an Address receives as is read from the metaflow and
; its AddressHold, never from an obligation.

Memory
[ signal_flow:[ LaunchRequestId StartRejection ReplaceRejection FlowId HerdrRoute Process NativeSessionId TranscriptPath BackgroundWork NativePrompt Address ReapStanding HandoverCloseRefusal HandoverOwner Successor ]
  flow_nexus:[ LaunchedRecord ReplacedRecord ]
  signal_flow:[ LogicalDeliveryId Metaflow Lock CallerIdentity LaunchAttempt StoreIdentity OrdinarySocketPath MetaSocketPath FlowType Origin HarnessKind EndpointSelection FlowLifecycle SessionId HerdrPaneId DeliverKey SendAcceptance DeliverySnapshot DeliveryCursor RequestId SentBy VisibleNativeInput Section Touch HerdrPaneBinding LaunchProfile TurnEnd UndecodableFrame Tokens ModelName HandoverGeneration ]
  meta_signal_flow:[ ConfigureNexus ConfigureModel ConfigureThreshold ConfigureSendServer ConfigureMetaflow ConfigureHarnessFlags HeartbeatConfig DrawBound TryBound HandoverPoliciesConfiguration HandoverArchiveConfiguration HandoverCountConfiguration Duration RestartRecord SendOutcomeRecord Delivery ProcessId ProcessUserId ProcessStartToken DeliveryId HarnessProfile MetaAspects MessageNexusPath RequestDigest QueueRequestId QueueAttemptId QueueEvidence AbsenceProof Undecided QueueResolutionRecord EveryMinutes ReminderText ]
  :meta_signal_flow:generated:signal:[ Path ]
  :std:boxed:[ Box ]
  flow_ethos:[ Minutes SourceRoot CodexEndpoint ] ]
[ LaunchOutcome.[ Started.LaunchedRecord
                  Replaced.ReplacedRecord
                  StartRejected.StartRejection
                  ReplaceRejected.ReplaceRejection
                  ; The successor is confirmed and receiving; its predecessor's
                  ; PendingReap stands.
                  ReapPending.ReplacedRecord
                  ; Started fresh; the PendingHandover at its Address names
                  ; this launch.
                  HandoverPending.LaunchedRecord
                  ; Final: a later launch at the Address took the handover over.
                  HandoverSuperseded.SupersededHandover ]
  SupersededHandover.{ Address HandoverOwner LaunchedRecord Successor }
  Replacement.{ LaunchRequestId Predecessor.String }
  ; The reap a predecessor is owed, keyed by the predecessor's FlowId; its
  ; successor is read through its launch's outcome; its responsibility says
  ; whose bearing events take it up.
  PendingReap.{ Predecessor LaunchRequestId Address ReapStanding ReapResponsibility }
  ; Who owes a pending reap: the flow its Address receives as, or the
  ; Address itself when nothing receives there. LaunchSuccessor is the
  ; successor its launch's outcome names; W3 writes it.
  ReapResponsibility.[ LaunchSuccessor
                       ; A later flow receiving at the Address took it over.
                       TakenOver.Responsible
                       ; No flow receives at the Address: the row's own
                       ; Address holds it.
                       AddressHeld ]
  Responsible.FlowId
  ; The handover owed at an Address to the flow a fresh launch made its
  ; receiving flow, keyed by the Address: one at most per Address.
  PendingHandover.{ Address HandoverOwner Successor LaunchRequestId HandoverCloseRefusal }
  SeatBirth.{ FlowId HerdrRoute Process }
  ; A recorded Stop holds its correlation and background-work metadata.
  RecordedStop.{ Option<NativeSessionId> Option<TranscriptPath> BackgroundWork }
  ; Harness metadata in report order, independent of transient transport.
  RecordedHarnessEvent.[ Started.Option<NativeSessionId>
                         ToolUsed.String
                         Stopped.RecordedStop
                         PromptSubmitted.NativePrompt
                         Ended.Option<NativeSessionId>
                         Cleared.Option<NativeSessionId> ]
  ; One flow's durable metadata; its original key is preserved exactly.
  FlowEvents.{ FlowId Vector<RecordedHarnessEvent> }
  ; The configuration Flow keeps for its meta clients, one family per kind;
  ; each row's key is written by hand beside it.
  StoredMetaNexusConfiguration.{ ConfigureNexus }
  ; The native model one Model runs, keyed by the Model.
  StoredMetaModelConfiguration.{ ConfigureModel }
  ; One model's refresh threshold, keyed by the model's name.
  StoredMetaThresholdConfiguration.{ ConfigureThreshold }
  StoredMetaSendServerConfiguration.{ ConfigureSendServer }
  StoredMetaMetaflowConfiguration.{ ConfigureMetaflow }
  ; The Address of the Investigation seat, one row.
  StoredMetaInvestigationConfiguration.{ Address }
  ; The default Minutes, one row; absent until Configure declares one.
  StoredMetaDefaultMinutesConfiguration.{ Minutes }
  StoredMetaRequestPolicyConfiguration.{ DrawBound TryBound }
  ; Extra native harness arguments for one metaflow, keyed by Address. An
  ; absent row means the empty argument string.
  StoredMetaHarnessFlagsConfiguration.{ ConfigureHarnessFlags }
  ; The configured sampling heartbeat; no row means disabled.
  StoredMetaHeartbeatConfiguration.{ HeartbeatConfig }
  ; The hook command a Claude flow is launched with, one row; none until a
  ; HarnessHook is declared.
  StoredMetaHarnessHookConfiguration.{ Path }
  ; One protected Address, one row per Address; none by default.
  StoredMetaProtectedAddressConfiguration.{ Address }
  StoredHandoverConfiguration.{ HandoverPoliciesConfiguration
                                HandoverArchiveConfiguration
                                HandoverCountConfiguration
                                Duration }
  ; The durable address-indexed Metaflow. Its state and queue are separate
  ; from native Flow launch records: an address remains asleep after the
  ; process it named is gone.
  StoredMetaflow.{ Metaflow }
  ; At most one lock is held for a recipient address.
  StoredMetaflowLock.{ Lock }
  ; A flow's role: its aspect and model, keyed by its FlowId. It is exactly
  ; what ResolveCaller answers, so the CallerIdentity is stored as it is.
  StoredRole.{ CallerIdentity }
  StoredLaunchAttempt.{ LaunchAttempt }
  StoredRestart.{ RestartRecord }
  StoredSendOutcome.{ SendOutcomeRecord }
  StoredDelivery.{ Delivery }
  StoredStoreIdentity.{ StoreIdentity }
  ; The sockets half of the meta Configuration.
  FlowStoreConfiguration.{ OrdinarySocketPath MetaSocketPath }
  ; The store's flow counter: the number the next flow is minted with.
  FlowStoreState.{ NextFlowNumber.Integer }
  ; One native flow's durable record, keyed by its FlowId: what launched it,
  ; its native thread once bound, its harness and endpoint, its lifecycle,
  ; and the generation of its seat.
  FlowRecord.{ FlowId
               FlowType
               Origin
               Option<SessionId>
               HarnessKind
               EndpointSelection
               FlowLifecycle
               Generation.Integer }
  ; The process that proved it owns a native session: its id, user and start
  ; token, the host and boot it ran on, its harness and the session.
  NativeOwnerProof.{ ProcessId
                     ProcessUserId
                     ProcessStartToken
                     HostId.String
                     BootId.String
                     HarnessKind
                     NativeSessionId }
  NativeOwnerProofRecord.{ FlowId NativeOwnerProof }
  ; A metaflow's process, keyed by its Address.
  StoredMetaflowProcess.{ Process Address }
  ; The Herdr route a flow's seat runs in, keyed by its FlowId.
  FlowHerdrRouteRecord.{ FlowId HerdrRoute }
  ; How a launch request settled, keyed by the request.
  StoredLaunchOutcome.{ LaunchRequestId LaunchOutcome }
  ; The Nexus's runtime half of the meta Configuration: its source root and
  ; its two Codex endpoints.
  RuntimeConfiguration.{ SourceRoot
                         StableCodex.CodexEndpoint
                         NextCodex.CodexEndpoint }
  ; The heartbeat's standing for one recipient, keyed by its Address: the
  ; evidence it last reported, the evidence seen since, and the reminder
  ; outstanding.
  StoredHeartbeatStanding.{ Address
                            BaselineAwake.Integer
                            BaselineWorking.Option<Integer>
                            BaselineWorkingComplete.Boolean
                            BaselineSent.Integer
                            BaselineQueue.Integer
                            LatestAwake.Integer
                            LatestWorking.Option<Integer>
                            LatestWorkingComplete.Boolean
                            LatestSent.Integer
                            LatestQueue.Integer
                            Option<LogicalDeliveryId> }
  ; Why a logical delivery was admitted: an ordinary send or the heartbeat.
  DeliveryPurpose.[ Ordinary Heartbeat ]
  ; How far a leased key sequence went: held with nothing sent yet, the
  ; interrupt keys sent, the text accepted by Herdr, the submit keys sent.
  LeaseStep.[ Acquired Interrupted Placed Submitted ]
  ; The lease one delivery holds on a pane, keyed by the delivery.
  PaneLease.{ DeliveryId FlowId HerdrPaneId LeaseStep }
  ; The delivery half of the meta Configuration, one row.
  DeliveryConfiguration.{ Vector<HarnessProfile> MetaAspects Option<MessageNexusPath> }
  ; A Deliver call answered, keyed by its DeliverKey: its sender, the digest
  ; of what it asked, and the answer a repeat gets.
  DeliverCall.{ DeliverKey Sender.Address RequestDigest SendAcceptance }
  ; Why one logical delivery was admitted, keyed by its id.
  LogicalDeliveryPurpose.{ LogicalDeliveryId Address DeliveryPurpose }
  ; The logical delivery counter: the cursor the next event takes.
  LogicalDeliveryCounter.{ NextCursor.Integer }
  ; How a logical delivery was admitted.
  DeliveryAdmission.[ Message Ordinary HistoricalUnknown ]
  ; A logical delivery as it stands, keyed by its id, with the cursor it
  ; was archived at, if it was.
  CurrentLogicalDelivery.{ DeliverySnapshot ArchivedCursor.Option<DeliveryCursor> DeliveryAdmission }
  ; One logical delivery event, keyed by its cursor.
  LogicalDeliveryEvent.{ DeliverySnapshot }
  ; A simplified flow's reply binding, keyed by its FlowId: the delivery it
  ; answers, who sent it, whom the reply goes to, and whether it is done.
  SimplifiedReplyBinding.{ FlowId InputDeliveryId.String Source.Address Recipient.Address Completed.Boolean }
  ; Whether a request is still open, or answered by a logical delivery.
  RequestClosure.[ Open Answered.LogicalDeliveryId ]
  ; A request id bound to its logical delivery, keyed by the request id.
  RequestIdBinding.{ RequestId LogicalDeliveryId RequestClosure }
  ; The queue delivery counters: the next request and attempt numbers.
  DeliveryCounter.{ NextRequest.Integer NextAttempt.Integer }
  ; Where a queued request stands. Unsent: its attempt was proved never to
  ; have reached the seat; it is still queued and a later attempt carries
  ; it. Parked: native history could not resolve it; it stays in the
  ; journal as Uncertain, no longer an active queue item, never handed over
  ; again automatically.
  RequestState.[ Queued Settled Unsent Parked ]
  ; One queued request, keyed by its id.
  StoredDeliveryRequest.{ QueueRequestId Address QueueEvidence RequestState }
  ; A native receipt: the native request, thread and turn, and the native
  ; response exactly as observed.
  NativeDeliveryReceipt.{ NativeRequestId.Integer ThreadId.String TurnId.String NativeReceiptText.String }
  ; Where native history stood before the text was typed: the Claude
  ; transcript and its length, or the Codex thread's newest turn, None when
  ; the thread had none.
  ; A Claude transcript file and its length: the device and inode it lives
  ; on and the byte offset its end stood at.
  NativeTranscriptCursor.{ Device.Integer Inode.Integer Offset.Integer }
  NativeHistoryAnchor.[ ClaudeTranscript.NativeTranscriptCursor CodexTurns.Option<String> ]
  ; Native history's proof that a request never reached the seat.
  AbsenceRecord.{ AbsenceProof Observation.String }
  ; Where one queue delivery attempt stands. Uncertain: native input may
  ; have reached the seat and no exact receipt is held; it is never sent
  ; again, the reason naming why the last reconciliation could not decide.
  ; Read: an authenticated answer proves the request read without an exact
  ; receipt; a receipt observed later stays separate. Absent: native history
  ; proved it never reached the seat. Resolved: the owner resolved an
  ; Uncertain attempt.
  QueueDeliveryPhase.[ Prepared
                       Uncertain.Option<Undecided>
                       ReceiptRecorded.NativeDeliveryReceipt
                       Settled.NativeDeliveryReceipt
                       Read.{ Answer.String LateReceipt.Option<NativeDeliveryReceipt> }
                       Absent.AbsenceRecord
                       Resolved.QueueResolutionRecord ]
  ; One attempt to deliver a queued request, keyed by the attempt.
  QueueDeliveryAttempt.{ QueueRequestId
                         QueueAttemptId
                         NativeRequestId
                         FlowId
                         ThreadId
                         HarnessKind
                         NativeHistoryAnchor
                         Address
                         QueueEvidence
                         QueueDeliveryPhase }
  ; The send outcome counter: the number the next outcome takes.
  SendOutcomeCounter.{ NextId.Integer }
  ; An answer kept for its request, keyed by the request id.
  KeptAnswer.{ RequestId VisibleNativeInput }
  ; One reminder asked for and not yet sent, keyed by its request id: whom it
  ; reminds, who asked, when it falls due in Unix seconds, and its words.
  ScheduledReminder.{ RequestId Address SentBy Due.Integer Text.String }
  ; What became of a compaction's investigation: the Investigation seat was
  ; started fresh with it as its brief; it was Awake and the investigation
  ; was queued for it; no Investigation seat is configured and the warning
  ; was logged only; or it could not be started or queued, and why.
  Investigation.[ Started.String Queued NotConfigured Refused.String ]
  ; One compaction a flow's harness reported, keyed by the flow and the
  ; harness's own id for it (a Claude compact_boundary row's uuid, a Codex
  ; contextCompaction item's id).
  Compaction.{ FlowId Boundary.String Option<Address> Investigation }
  ; A flow's context size, keyed by its FlowId.
  FlowContextSize.{ FlowId Tokens }
  ; The exact pane created for a launch before its harness is asked to
  ; start, keyed by the launch request.
  StoredLaunchPane.{ HerdrPaneBinding HarnessStartRequested.Boolean Orphaned.Boolean }
  ; An Address's handover, keyed by the Address: the sections now written,
  ; their touch, the generation, the flow writing it, and the generations
  ; closed before.
  HandoverMemory.{ Address
                   Vector<Section>
                   Option<Touch>
                   HandoverGeneration
                   Option<FlowId>
                   Vector<ClosedHandover> }
  ; One closed handover generation: its predecessor and successor and what
  ; it held.
  ClosedHandover.{ HandoverGeneration Predecessor Successor Vector<Section> Option<Touch> }
  ; The handover reminders of one generation at an Address, keyed by both:
  ; the model, when the warning window opened (Unix seconds), when the next
  ; reminder is due (the first at the opening, inclusive), how many were
  ; admitted, their interval and their words. A successor uses a new row.
  HandoverReminder.{ Address
                     HandoverGeneration
                     ModelName
                     OpenedAt.Integer
                     NextDue.Integer
                     Sent.Integer
                     EveryMinutes
                     ReminderText }
  ; Whether a launch cleanup step has succeeded: Pending is taken again by
  ; the next start, Done never.
  CleanupStep.[ Pending Done ]
  ; What a launch's cleanup owes, keyed by the launch request: the thread it
  ; opened, and whether that thread and its pane are cleaned up.
  LaunchCleanup.{ LaunchRequestId NativeSessionId ThreadStep.CleanupStep PaneStep.CleanupStep }
  ; The thread a launch opened, keyed by the launch request.
  OpenedLaunchThread.{ LaunchRequestId NativeSessionId }
  ; A launch ordered as a replacement's successor, with the first prompt's
  ; digest as its profile composed it when ordered.
  OrderedLaunch.{ LaunchProfile Origin PromptSha256.String }
  ; What a replacement was ordered as: a Refresh, whose successor is what
  ; any refresh starts; a Launch or Replace, its own profile the successor;
  ; or a Restart, the flow's harness closed and its own session resumed.
  ReplacementOrder.[ Refresh Launch.Box<OrderedLaunch> Restart ]
  ; A replacement ordered at an Address, keyed by the Address.
  OrderedReplacement.{ Address Predecessor ReplacementOrder }
  ; One open Task's reminders, keyed by the task's LogicalDeliveryId: the
  ; metaflow reminded (its sender), the metaflow it was sent to, its Minutes
  ; (its first deadline and every interval after), when the next reminder
  ; is due in Unix seconds (None once it has had all its reminders, or set
  ; none, its sender unknown), and how many were sent.
  Reminder.{ LogicalDeliveryId Address Recipient Minutes Option<Due> Sent }
  ; Why a successor is owed: its flow passed its refresh threshold and
  ; rested; it ended without Flow or an owner ending it, its pane gone; a
  ; Refresh ordered from outside ended it; or a Replace ended it, its
  ; successor the Replace's own launch.
  SuccessionCause.[ Refresh Exit Ordered Replace ]
  ; The successor an Address is owed, keyed by the Address.
  SuccessorIntent.{ Address Predecessor SuccessionCause LaunchRequestId }
  ; One turn end a harness reported, keyed by its turn.
  TurnEndRecord.{ TurnEndKey.String TurnEnd }
  ; One frame a caller sent that did not decode, keyed by the nanoseconds
  ; since the Unix epoch, zero-padded, then the caller's process id.
  UndecodableRecord.{ UndecodableKey.String UndecodableFrame }
  ; The flow a launch holds an Address for, keyed by its FlowId, with the
  ; metaflow found there when it was held.
  AddressHold.{ FlowId Address Option<Metaflow> } ]
